Id: ssh006f
Severity: FAIL
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set PermitRootLogin no (prohibit-password for key-based automation).
References: sshd_config(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

PermitRootLogin is yes, so root may log in over SSH with a password,
which puts the one account every attacker tries behind a guessable
secret. Set it to no, or to prohibit-password if root needs key-based
access for automation.
